Fuzzing

lfuzz is an AFL++ harness. Each target is a Lua script that returns a
function of one input string. An error that escapes the function is a
bug: the harness aborts. Targets catch expected errors themselves.

  json         lgml.json, OpenAI request checks, the chat templates
  chat         the Hermes and Gemma-4 output parsers on model text
  http         request heads, query strings, multipart bodies
  safetensors  lgml.safetensors, then a load to the CPU backend
  vocab        lgml.vocab on vocab.json and added_tokens.json
  wav          WAV decode, encode, resample and mel
  tokenize     all pre-tokenizers (qwen2, llama-bpe, gemma4) on tiny
               vocabs; round trips

Run all targets for 10 minutes (needs afl-clang-fast and luarocks):

  fuzz/run.sh 600

This builds build-fuzz with afl-clang-fast, ASan and UBSan, and builds
lua-cjson and picohttpparser the same way. The harness uses only the
CPU backend; no Vulkan driver loads. Crashes land in
build-fuzz/out/<target>/default/crashes. Replay one:

  fuzz/run.sh replay json build-fuzz/out/json/default/crashes/id:...

After a fix, copy the crash into corpus/<target>/. The normal build
replays the corpus in the 'fuzz' test suite:

  meson test -C build --suite fuzz

seeds.lua writes the seed corpus. dict/ holds the AFL dictionaries.
